      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i live in one of the new high-rise developments downtown and i'm having a really hard time sleeping. there's this constant low hum or vibration coming from the HVAC/smart lighting system. it's not a normal noise, it feels like it's hitting a specific frequency that just makes my skin crawl and keeps me in this state of high anxiety. i've been tracking the patterns when the lights dim and it seems intentional. do you know anything about how these smart systems use infrasound or specific frequencies for building management? it feels like it's being used to keep the residents in a certain 'mood'.",
