      "content": "i tried the app but the phone mic doesn't seem to pick up the low stuff effectively, it just shows silence even though i can literally feel the vibration in my chest and it's making me feel so paranoid. if this is actually being used to manage resident \"moods\" or compliance, does that mean it's a deliberate design choice by the developers? i'm starting to wonder if there's a way to shield my apartment or block these specific frequencies so i can actually have some peace. what kind of materials or setups would even work against something like this?",
